Thanks to Joe Fletcher and Keith Strange for their responses.  Joe Fletchers
response is the one that did the trick.
 
"Think you've got it slightly inverted. Should read "lan_config -ialt0 -a0"
to disable autonegotiation. There are no console settings for the DEGPA
cards. You can include the lan_config line in /etc/inet.local."
 
Right now I am auto-negotiating at 1000 Full.  I will this out when I am
able to take the cards down.
 
Thanks again,
 
Chris
 



Admins, 

        I have a gs140 running 5.1 pk 3.  On this box I have 2 DEGPA gigabit
interfaces.  The 2 cards will auto-negotiate to 1000Mb/full-duplex but
management wants me to set these to non-auto, 1000Mb/full-duplex.  I used
lan_config -i alt0 -a 1 -x 0 to accomplish this, however, I was not able to
connect via this link.  I think that there may have been a duplex problem
with the port being set to half-duplex but just to verify on our end I have
2 questions.

        1.  Is the above command what you execute to disable
auto-negotiation and set to full duplex? 

        2.  How can I hard code these cards at the P00>>> prompt? 

TIA, 

Chris Bryant 
Unix Administrator 
Dollar Rent A Car 
(918) 669-3213 


------_=_NextPart_001_01C1A9CB.05D00A60
