....I forgot to tell how you extract the specific files from the media
(Ass. Products Vol. 2), as descriped by Jason Orendorf:

# cd /var/cluster/caa/monitors/
# cp tape.so tape.so.pk4
# cp changer.so changer.so.pk4
# cp network.so network.so.pk4
# cd /usr/sbin
# cp caad caad.pk4

Mount the Associated Products CD that contains the
TruCluster kit, and locate the file called "TCRBASE510".
setld subset files are simply compressed tar files, so
just do:

# cd /
# gzip -dc /mnt/PATH_TO_TCR_KIT/TCRBASE510 | tar -xf - \
  ./var/cluster/caa/monitors/tape.so \
  ./var/cluster/caa/monitors/network.so \
  ./var/cluster/caa/monitors/changer.so ./usr/sbin/caad

Compaq recommends you copy the pk4-files back before you install a new
patchkit later on, ie pk5.

Greetings
Danny Petteson



