Thanks go out to Dan Harrington and Udo de Boer for their aid.

After talking to our developers the action taken is to be decided upon.  I
have made the following suggestions as I examined some of the suggestions
given.  Although I can't yet give the results of each... 

1.) Modify the socket listen queue limits - opening up more sockets
2.) Enable keepalive functionality - this cleans up sockets that do not exit
cleanly when the keepalive interval expires.
*3.) Decrease the TCP Connection Context Timeout limit - shortens the life
of a wait state for the tcp connection

**4.) Dis-able the PMTU discovery - the PMTU(path maximum transmission unit)
if a system has many remote clients this is suggested as the system creates
routing information for each client network.

* needs to be tested...
**not really related to the problem, but could improve performance on the
system.

