From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jan 22 03:22:09 2002
From: "Neil McCoy" <Neil.McCoy () afp ! gov ! au>
Date: Tue, 22 Jan 2002 03:22:09 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Oracle 8.1.7 and above on EV5 chipset
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653723421966


My company had the slow performance problem for about 6 months, with
calls logged to both
Oracle and COMPAQ.

Finally, Oracle admitted that only some EV5 chips fully support Oracle
8.1.7.
EV5 chips below about 330MHz lack new commands introduced in faster
chips.
Thus, EV5 chips up to 330Mhz runOracle 8.1.7  impossibly slowly in
EV5/6 emulation mode.
Machines running EV5 chips @ 466MHz or faster at my company all worked
fine.


